I figured that an English muffin isn't actually English just like a
French fry isn't actually French (pommes frites from Brussels).

Called Toaster biscuits by Australians an English muffin is a bread
that appears to be cooked on a grill because it is flat and one
side has more bubbles and the other side has bits of coarse corn
meal to keep it from sticking.  They must be cooked inside a ring
to form their exactly circular shape.

A regular muffin in America is as dogscoff described.  A wet soft
dough with various flavors cooked in a cupcake mold.

